// Stubs for the APIs LG adds by patching framework.jar itself. We cannot ship
// their framework.jar, so the classes the stock apps reach for live here
// instead and go on the boot classpath next to it. Same idea as
// hardware/oneplus/oneplus-fwk.
//
// Most are com.lge.*, but not all: AudioManagerEx and friends sit in the
// platform's own packages, so src/android/ is part of this too. That is what
// the boot jar buys - the runtime resolves by name across the whole
// classpath, so a class named android.media.AudioManagerEx is found here
// whether or not framework.jar has one.
//
// Only what the apps actually call is implemented: the surface comes from
// diffing the classes their smali references against the boot classpath this
// builds, so anything in here is something a shipped app would have died on.
java_library {
    name: "com.lge",
    installable: true,

    srcs: [
        "src/**/*.java",
    ],
}
